[{"id":"VRCE-6-39-1","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":39,"verse":1,"english":"Bound up terribly with shafts, Dasaratha's sons, lying down bathed in blood, sighed hard like to serpents.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.873,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-49-1"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6039001","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"0f8b005e6507923d9e8d5140362b80116a620e988e07d78be9686a34cce0b0ba","compact":"b0ca04d34c1ff776c25775a06c5a5aae63f0ce41764c2b8393de587a2113c817","nasal":"c7a021467f6b857531f63425795968dd803cac017a8e41dd5da21b3589ef3edd"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-39-2","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":39,"verse":2,"english":"All those foremost monkeys, along with Sugrīva, possessed of exceeding strength, overwhelmed with sorrow, remained surrounding those high-souled ones.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.877,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-49-2"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6039002","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"d6a64b988b0ec705cd9239c958410d0fe9406fa846722a74a2783f7f30c59377","compact":"b80d19d99ad94173541f3888c9c97fb87f5b8298246ead95089e7cd3609f1799","nasal":"b80d19d99ad94173541f3888c9c97fb87f5b8298246ead95089e7cd3609f1799"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-39-3","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":39,"verse":3,"english":"In the meanwhile, the powerful Rāma, albeit fast bound by the shafts, awoke by virtue of the exceeding toughness of his person, as well as his might.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.797,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-49-3"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6039003","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"6b20dafcdc070eec8de74f8c101d6da0f3ba2b09eddf4c4f13f9be1cd5f684e7","compact":"49c55e9340cb777b16e6584813f429c718c4a98d2f5851a235abb02dfa533f4f","nasal":"59b07a7fa08e5f23844c3360b5751b93c5a4bdf44b21fcb59411f67eff53c4dd"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-39-4","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":39,"verse":4,"english":"Then, seeing his brother having a distressful countenance, covered with blood, feeble, and fast bound by the shafts, Rāma, greatly aggrieved, began to mourn.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.86,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-49-4"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6039004","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"8a5a55af18b048c0bf23ba72712335ddc08d94ad65116608c7359d5dea967978","compact":"a8f4d27d2d3dc0e3624ac776305deca5f26ff5bb7b6b196be309078b34ef6057","nasal":"2b6a3c8b5c1f02c921258fa4ddf32bf533ce7d11d06c594edac2ebadaabb06df"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-39-5","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":39,"verse":5,"english":"Of what use to me is the recovery of Sītă, or life either, when today I see my brother vanquished in fight and lying down in the field?","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.682,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-49-5"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6039005","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"233a0e7c3cd433e6096db54d3053fcbfbbc09ada4960953c48c81363d95cca98","compact":"4a751fcfe8063fb532ffa3634091978bcf7c48ef9e09a577cc0550dcdac2a7eb","nasal":"4a751fcfe8063fb532ffa3634091978bcf7c48ef9e09a577cc0550dcdac2a7eb"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-39-6","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":39,"verse":6,"english":"Seeking in the world (of men), I may light upon a woman like Sītā; but never on a brother, or a helper, or a warrior like to Laksmana.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.609,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-49-6"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6039006","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"cb96078ec10bbac437bffb84d1dccc4eb04f2408eeceb04163b4bd9e1424652c","compact":"c3e72a6835c61a454cefcba5b3f3aa6610928e88bd21cfe179ed3b5855064b50","nasal":"5b9867d604a26b52541ad0d5f8cbf0f337c86e8e62ac7e3078d0310a18d47958"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-39-7","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":39,"verse":7,"english":"If that enhancer of Sumitra's joy have met with his end, my life I must renounce in the sight of the monkeys.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-49-7"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6039007","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"8c4eb890938ec2ac59b84ffaf179d1076abad0d02028495ad04849e81fdc1bb0","compact":"9cb83f4abaf2d9ab6a55cbbae8faa9c9786296f4781734a9d04824993896b0f6","nasal":"060fdf58cdb58be17c9ac3f481cbd75a4b92e07e01b04119057189729a1eaeab"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-39-8","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":39,"verse":8,"english":"What shall I say to Kausalyā; and what shall I say to Kaikeyi ? And what shall I say to mother Sumitrā eager for a sight of her son? And if I go (back) without him, how shall I soothe her, like to a cow reft of her calf; and trembling; and resembling a mourning Kurari?","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-49-8"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6039008","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"6313373b878a77749cb20d8e47c995d77fc8d15d22a38ed51619f0945f805133","compact":"e86682e04f4b28b47c8f63f1f06a25a649b4ed4cb2b6e4b8271bbe10b502fd60","nasal":"c8ccce46777984e365c251519ae315f8e96aa2924d95fed16a1f958858c61830"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-39-9","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":39,"verse":9,"english":"What shall I say to Kausalyā; and what shall I say to Kaikeyi ? And what shall I say to mother Sumitrā eager for a sight of her son? And if I go (back) without him, how shall I soothe her, like to a cow reft of her calf; and trembling; and resembling a mourning Kurari?","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.726,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-49-8"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6039009","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"b760cee415f6b9e069aaf9b32139b35644eda54fc257edf381ea1517ed1e8175","compact":"9ed19587799298b62e3910053097d156b91dafa65868e2d7633f939119ade392","nasal":"2158da0b623c4a6a630f09e00d0e8a904a78b8a7fdd0f376632fde788a961ed9"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-39-10","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":39,"verse":10,"english":"How shall I say to Satrughna and the illustrious Bharata, 'He went with me to the forest; but I come (back) here without him \"?","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.873,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-49-9"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6039010","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"fb07b81c3eae33fc2d4da7f66b0b9dfe44547b91df03bb224130192a190fea24","compact":"a475661d21f07ba6683babd1b4e8452f2313c6c6c94572e2ce57954178ffa522","nasal":"89a116bcb0914435984adb950e9ad5a256dc5527a81a0ce86c33a41e4cf63463"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-39-11","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":39,"verse":11,"english":"I shall not be able to bear the rebuke of mother Sumitră. Therefore even here shall I renounce my person; for certainly I dare not live.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.839,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-49-10"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6039011","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"50392082f8390de340048d28b3bcde5d8e3de93f45c5f20cb98c31d2c35aa1c8","compact":"f65aeccb483c323e2ca5c8a87f952b09063be1deafe88f1e08723b2762d32bc7","nasal":"a93c9a011d7ea320c9555cb280f8356ebb77ad2c5658ea9b4d1a9552937b6289"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-39-12","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":39,"verse":12,"english":"Fie on me, who am wicked and base; for me this Lakşmaņa, brought down, leith in the field of battle, like one that is without life.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.703,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-49-11"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6039012","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"f7cb028d85390141e3b92758dbd7e640543f3eb3876b7ec331336309d535677c","compact":"15553993bab366b5b8dc4213657728bffa1a4fb6889420d89192b2c34a223dab","nasal":"15553993bab366b5b8dc4213657728bffa1a4fb6889420d89192b2c34a223dab"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-39-13","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":39,"verse":13,"english":"O Lakşmaņa, you ever comforts me when I am dispirited. But today, having lost your life, you can not speak to me, who am afflicted.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.853,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-49-12"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6039013","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"4b0dc67bc90807c02ab6f13d37b2ef5873a61ed7d5db1d3dd77548521b7f43b8","compact":"f7f545669e19506648610b69dd14323c0a8171d62f35a6248cf918ca684ff3ce","nasal":"be700ec75da293f108a4d0460fa890dc1b865e4acc399e062b1813b2db6618c8"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-39-14","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":39,"verse":14,"english":"You, O hero, who had in battle slain innumerable Rākṣasa lying around, have (at length) yourself been slain in the field with shafts.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.311,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-49-13"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6039014","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"dc929769785c4cacc7ad0b961223f2b3fe301269095b4ca6cb82984ecaba0d96","compact":"370a42b67d5ddadd4ef63e35874ac9b5303f44d4fda22b4f04dc7f1ca743420d","nasal":"370a42b67d5ddadd4ef63e35874ac9b5303f44d4fda22b4f04dc7f1ca743420d"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-39-15","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":39,"verse":15,"english":"And lying down in the battle-field, bleeding and covered with arrows, you appear like the Sun when he has gone up the Setting-hill.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.413,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-49-14"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6039015","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"79f5ff78404dc710f13785cfb594463f062e54751ec1886511d4c5ee1415b752","compact":"5c74304e8690764f6f754428926d84a4d552cffc8ba61e692d52b1d508b68c38","nasal":"5c74304e8690764f6f754428926d84a4d552cffc8ba61e692d52b1d508b68c38"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-39-16","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":39,"verse":16,"english":"In consequence of shafts piercing your vitals, you cannot speak; but your visible expression, albeit you are dumb, betokens pain.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.638,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-49-15"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6039016","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"3e396d138b2553a3b02a24959393ad7264504e4af56ed963fbb01af9de151c53","compact":"37d78dacf3182ad638c426419a268fe9a6b8a8847f1e100c738d276de5acd4ff","nasal":"4f44da60c0d946f90da6993d94c66377d4ecf4317d0733772ccb2da11794884c"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-39-17","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":39,"verse":17,"english":"O you endowed with exceeding splendour, even as you did follow me into the forest, will I follow you to the mansion of Yama.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-49-16"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6039017","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"7f597015a3af480bbb6d177541d2fd6221d2f4ff7980bc943b15cee33b4485b0","compact":"9dd8099e0bd8205b51830fe1e109b00924e05ce8dff62253e6549f8886e5b91a","nasal":"e6b52fcd1037cd2502204dfa1e8b1bb8e93a48f8d1415aad3e6ce1c161e1231f"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-39-18","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":39,"verse":18,"english":"You having dear friends, and ever following me, has come by this plight in consequence of my reprehensible conduct.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-49-17"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6039018","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"2d224fd85ea3eeeb2e52f06aed7a4fbf269c558618068943c6f9b7803302e4c6","compact":"b1001690bf6ba25c7a98d93ff310f517e94d0a6a5b2aa28a6e50c52057acc377","nasal":"32552f954a53ff22a70b528cda6104de75e4076b60fe105b119ae5ccdec2dded"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-39-19","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":39,"verse":19,"english":"I do not remember having heard any harsh speech from the heroic Lakşmaņa, even when he had happened to be exceedingly wroth.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.627,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-49-18"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6039019","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"fc5bdd0819e3216845fff79b44ac02d4d7a97b7616098b3e12317211bc3b1315","compact":"75f9db81788e957fa2dfcd77fcf210e808bf45d73a3d57e81a436b1b21269c48","nasal":"75f9db81788e957fa2dfcd77fcf210e808bf45d73a3d57e81a436b1b21269c48"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-39-20","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":39,"verse":20,"english":"He that could discharge at one shot five hundred shafts, that Lakşmaņa is superior to karttaviryya himself in that weapon-the bow.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.882,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-49-19"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6039020","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"f39d280c507104ed304fec142876a3cf424962ea0df3140a1fd78d16690e4a52","compact":"50f3009e86a7837d999fea2b8e0949360c28de1f5c946bc1620edad3ec6ac41f","nasal":"1315d2496bd4f547e3cf2f2d39bcb3baf5304efb75ebda85cd84af10db5e64ed"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-39-21","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":39,"verse":21,"english":"He that with his arms could resist the arms of Sakra himself, that one worthy of a costly couchLeith down on the ground, slain.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.681,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-49-20"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6039021","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"b89dbff1327dea5a0cce1b85f741d496f82397bc94bf8730cd9a534791caa5a7","compact":"5635bea019f7d8eb214c825afcb7c71b827496d08a0d175c3876ffaf4225a575","nasal":"5635bea019f7d8eb214c825afcb7c71b827496d08a0d175c3876ffaf4225a575"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-39-22","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":39,"verse":22,"english":"That false babble shall now, without doubt, consume me; for by me has not Bibhishna been made monarch of the Rákşasas.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.937,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-49-21"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6039022","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"a39db5f95079d25907e93edd7a625f5f5f617cac78ee9d27afdd71dff1636209","compact":"31de62d172fce53522e5e5c26aa226cc1757e99c4c08ef418b54d10f6320231c","nasal":"31de62d172fce53522e5e5c26aa226cc1757e99c4c08ef418b54d10f6320231c"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-39-23","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":39,"verse":23,"english":"Do you, O Sugrīva, this very moment retrace your steps. Bereft of your strength through me you will be worsted by Rāvaņa.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.433,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-49-22"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6039023","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"97185a74f2a707d76c916ba71feba738b91275dbe9139914e3689795bc02cef6","compact":"2779efeac8a489a77c120f4142f2fddf5b7dd3f08aefff041e13eda251f72b0b","nasal":"2779efeac8a489a77c120f4142f2fddf5b7dd3f08aefff041e13eda251f72b0b"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-39-24","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":39,"verse":24,"english":"O Sugriva, placing Angada to the fore, do you, taking your host as well as the equipage, in company with Nila and Nala, cross over the Ocean.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.414,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-49-23"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6039024","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"fdd9ac8307af017b033bb165f20fb01b2fb73a4dd3a91166901350de54016e07","compact":"4d96e1324f3f8f14fc100e90d04c95d5d7e01bb982dfc972c94651fc25a3e1b0","nasal":"744e89e3eea59452a307346460b4000c298336aabc36882ed0baf9062ff4ff4a"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-39-25","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":39,"verse":25,"english":"By you has been achieved a mighty feat incapable of being done by another in battle. And pleased am I with the king of bears, and the lord of Golãngulas; and Angada has quit himself nobly, as also Mainda and Dvivida. And Kesarin and Sampāti have both faught terribly.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.6,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-49-24"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6039025","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"06b466dc2bd2b1bf5dca3e22e1884329e14545a9ae3c9c430bf1d991b29fd713","compact":"98c756bb059ba88148e22c180947835ff9f42393b3e46c40b3f61a6bfa2246ee","nasal":"4d5c743cabfc37bce097e163d5865a5c4ca1c60b21486084c648b67dcfc45b44"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-39-26","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":39,"verse":26,"english":"By you has been achieved a mighty feat incapable of being done by another in battle. And pleased am I with the king of bears, and the lord of Golãngulas; and Angada has quit himself nobly, as also Mainda and Dvivida. And Kesarin and Sampāti have both faught terribly.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.869,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-49-24"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6039026","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"f01538bff39b85676e2619eff3b2497fb82d83adb11a49f6b3d558bbc83f3113","compact":"8a7c29333012c97bbe2f77e0d04f6c878df47b6ffddd8635497bc14b6190e137","nasal":"91f1d8c821d295641c3502a64b7dc7ca5000edf6c5786ad2e17c341facc12527"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-39-27","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":39,"verse":27,"english":"Gavaya, and Gavākşa, and Sarabha, and Gaja, and other monkeys have faught as others are incapable of fighting, determined to lay down their lives (for me).","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.614,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-49-25"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6039027","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"afe783880e3ab60bb3463a59a98f504970fd39ae9e4bab8c8c87e817448fe914","compact":"5b2216ec19fbfefb242f50341bbd9ee1fbf1eafcd7e2083ac936de5cf9399407","nasal":"5b2216ec19fbfefb242f50341bbd9ee1fbf1eafcd7e2083ac936de5cf9399407"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-39-28","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":39,"verse":28,"english":"But, O Sugriva, man cannot overrule Destiny. You, my friend, fearing righteousness, has done what lay in your power. And, You foremost of monkeys, you also have acted as become friends. Now, with my permission, go you whitersoever you are minded.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.902,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-49-26"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":